From f1cb453067e007485ee0230c6bcfdc8de8295de9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DSF PC Port <jmokikearns@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:38:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] Render passes for embedding hosts; SPU register reads
 inside passes

An embedding host (PSX_EMBED) is handed one image per VBlank, so temporal
passes there are presented by render_pass_embed.c: a pass image replaces
the readout on its VBlank once the display flips to its rect, at least
shown_after_vblanks after the plan. The VRAM transaction is the OpenGL
renderer's own (gl_renderer_embed_pass_*, no presenter needed) or, with the
software renderer, a whole-VRAM backup plus the hi-res rect.

SPU registers are read in a pass as of its start: the SPU is caught up on
the live clock before the freeze and spu_read() does not catch up while a
pass runs. The transfer FIFO is still refused.

Tests: render_pass_abort/sandbox link again (g_boot_state_cpu_timing_restored
stub) and cover SPU reads; SPU tests define g_psx_render_pass_active.
